*> PLB-Q031 set-to-itself: an SQL UPDATE that sets a column to itself.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. SETSELF.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
    EXEC SQL INCLUDE SQLCA END-EXEC.
    EXEC SQL DECLARE ACCOUNT TABLE
        (ACCT_ID CHAR(10) NOT NULL, BALANCE DECIMAL(11,2),
         BRANCH CHAR(4))
    END-EXEC.
01  WS-ID               PIC X(10).
01  BALANCE             PIC S9(9)V99 COMP-3.
01  WS-BRANCH           PIC X(4).
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    *> Reported: BALANCE = BALANCE, alone and before another column.
    EXEC SQL UPDATE ACCOUNT SET BALANCE = BALANCE
        WHERE ACCT_ID = :WS-ID END-EXEC
    EXEC SQL UPDATE ACCOUNT SET BALANCE = BALANCE, BRANCH = :WS-BRANCH
        WHERE ACCT_ID = :WS-ID END-EXEC
    *> Not reported: a host variable of the same name, an expression,
    *> and another column.
    EXEC SQL UPDATE ACCOUNT SET BALANCE = :BALANCE
        WHERE ACCT_ID = :WS-ID END-EXEC
    EXEC SQL UPDATE ACCOUNT SET BALANCE = BALANCE + 1
        WHERE ACCT_ID = :WS-ID END-EXEC
    EXEC SQL UPDATE ACCOUNT SET BRANCH = ACCT_ID
        WHERE ACCT_ID = :WS-ID END-EXEC
    IF SQLCODE NOT = 0
        DISPLAY SQLCODE
    END-IF
    STOP RUN.
